<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gung Ye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/918">918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gung Ye was a warlord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>'s Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>, said to be an outcast Silla prince who lost an eye as an infant and became a Buddhist monk. He rose as a rebel commander and in 901 proclaimed a kingdom, later called Majin and then Taebong, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheorwon">Cheorwon</a>. Claiming to be the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maitreya">Maitreya Buddha</a>, he grew increasingly tyrannical and was overthrown in 918 by his generals, who made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-goryeo">Wang Geon</a> king of Goryeo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gung-ye.jpg" alt="Gung Ye" width="282" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (Wikibotbot) 위키봇봇 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EA%B6%81%EC%98%88.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
